1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
Good morning. I'd like to open a bank account, please.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:07,640
Certainly. If you'd like to take a seat, I'll just get some details from you

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,750
It won't take long. Thanks.

4
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:15,200
Is it a current account or a deposit account you wanted? A current account.

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,420
Right. I've got the application form here then

6
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:23,360
We have different types. I see you've got our leaflet there.

7
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:25,920
I've decided on the one called 'Select.'

8
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:30,530
Right, that's fine, so, first of all, can I have your full name please?

9
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:35,850
Yes, it's Pieter Henes. That's P. I-E-T-E-R.

10
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:38,600
Is it H-E-double N-E-S?

11
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:42,600
Uh, only one N actually. It's a less common spelling of the name.

12
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:46,910
Oh, right. OK. And what's your date of birth please?

13
00:00:46,910 --> 00:00:50,600
The twenty-seventh of the first, nineteen seventy-three.

14
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:55,870
Right. And will this be a joint account? No, just myself.

15
00:00:55,870 --> 00:01:01,700
OK, fine. And where are you living, Mr. Henes? 15. Riverside.

16
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:05,900
Is that all one word? Yes. Exeter? Yes.

17
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:11,340
How long have you been at your present address? Er, is it more than two years?

18
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:13,280
Ah, just two weeks actually

19
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:17,080
I only arrived in the country a month ago. I'm from Holland.

20
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:21,420
Oh, that's fine. But we normally ask for a previous address in that case.

21
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:31,950
Oh yes, well, it's Rielsdorf 2. That's R. I-E-L-S-D-O-R-F 2, Utrecht.

22
00:01:31,950 --> 00:01:38,430
Holland. OK. Thank you. Do you have a daytime telephone number?

23
00:01:38,430 --> 00:01:46,449
Yes, I think the number at my office is six-oh-six-two-nine-five. Um, just a minute, I'd better check.

24
00:01:46,449 --> 00:01:52,840
Oh no sorry, six- one-six. I'm not used to it yet

25
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:54,940
Would you like my home number too?

26
00:01:54,940 --> 00:02:00,040
Yes please. It's seven-nine-six-four-three-one.

27
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:02,830
Are they both local numbers? Yes.

28
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:07,640
Right. And your occupation?

29
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:12,160
Well, I'm in Britain as a project manager, but that's not my main job

30
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:14,360
I'm an engineer by profession.

31
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:17,620
I see. I think I'll put that then. It's shorter

32
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:20,799
Now we usually ask for a piece of information

33
00:02:20,799 --> 00:02:24,420
which we can use to check your identity, for security reasons

34
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,560
You know, if you phone us.

35
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:28,960
Like, erm, my wife's first name?

36
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:32,540
Mother's might be better. It's less likely to be known.

37
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:39,600
OK. Hers is Siti. Siti? Yes, S. I-T. I. It's Indonesian.

38
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:44,020
Fine. And how much would you like to open your account with?

39
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:48,440
We usually ask for a minimum sum of £50. That's about €75.

40
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:53,745
Well, I'm going to transfer €2,000 from my Dutch account, just till I get paid.

41
00:02:53,745 --> 00:02:59,050
In fact, I wanted to ask you about that. What's the best way to do it?

42
00:02:59,050 --> 00:03:01,230
It depends which bank you're with.

43
00:03:01,230 --> 00:03:03,620
It's the Fransen Bank in Utrecht.

44
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:05,920
OK, fine. I'll check that in a minute

45
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:09,130
If we have links with them we can do a direct transfer.

46
00:03:09,130 --> 00:03:13,200
But it's not a big problem either way. Um, let's see

47
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:15,650
How often would you like to receive statements?

48
00:03:15,650 --> 00:03:19,570
I haven't really thought. Um, what's the usual thing?

49
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:22,030
It's up to you. Some people like them weekly.

50
00:03:22,030 --> 00:03:26,870
Oh, no, that's too often. Can I have them sent, um, once a month?

51
00:03:26,870 --> 00:03:29,710
Yes, that's fine. Is there anything else?

52
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:33,870
I was thinking of registering for your internet service at some stage.

53
00:03:33,870 --> 00:03:38,690
Oh, yes. Would you like me to send you information about that? Please, yes.

54
00:03:38,690 --> 00:03:43,370
And would you like to receive information about the bank's other services -

55
00:03:43,370 --> 00:03:45,320
insurance, loans, anything like that?

56
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:47,400
Hmm, I don't think so, thanks.

57
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:51,670
That's OK then. And one last thing, if you agree...
